<title>Network.fetchJson Action</title>


<subheader>Format</subheader>


<logicsyntax>
s = CS.Network.fetchJson(<arg>url</arg> := ...
                      『, <arg>method</arg> := ...』
                      『, <arg>headers</arg> := ...』
                      『, <arg>body</arg> := ...』『, <arg>bodyFormat</arg> := ...』
                      『, <arg>detailed</arg> := ...』
                      『, <arg>responseHeadersFormat</arg> := ...』)
</logicsyntax>

<indent><table 3 header nowrap>
    <cell>Argument</cell><cell>Description</cell><cell nowrap>Types / Required</cell>
    <cell><arg>url</arg></cell><cell>The URL to fetch.</cell><cell>string~!~required</cell>
    <include fetch_arguments_optional.hgi />
</table></indent>


<subheader>Description</subheader>

The <action>Network.fetchJson</action> <link action_invoker.csdoc>action</link> submits a HTTP request to a server and returns the response, with or without details, in <link JSON_primer.csdoc>JSON</link> format.

This action is a wrapper around the actions <action>Network.fetch</action> and <action>Network.fetchBody</action>. <include fetch_convenience_methods.hgi />


<include fetch_url.hgi />

<include fetch_method.hgi />

<include fetch_headers.hgi />

<include fetch_body.hgi />

<include fetch_detailed_response.hgi />


<subheader>Return Value</subheader>

By default, the action returns the HTTP response body parsed as JSON, returning a string, number, boolean, array, or object. If <arg>detailed</arg> is <logiccolor>true</logiccolor>, the action returns an object with the response body as parsed JSON and details about the response as described above.


<subheader>Exceptions</subheader>

The action throws an exception if any of its arguments are not specified in a valid form, or if:

<list>
    <include fetch_exceptions.hgi />
    <li>The response is not valid JSON.</li>
</list>


<subheader>Example (JavaScript)</subheader>

<color JavaScript>
// display information about latest few CSPro releases;
// the GitHub API requires the specification of a User-Agent header
CS.Network.fetchJsonAsync({
    url: "https://api.github.com/repos/csprousers/cspro/releases?page=1&per_page=5",
    headers: [
        "User-Agent: CSPro Help Documentation Example"
    ]
})
.then(releases => {
    // the releases endpoint returns an array of objects
    releases.forEach(release => {
        console.log(
            `Release tagged '${release.tag_name}' ` +
            `authored by '${release.author.login}' ` +
            `created at '${release.created_at}'`
        );
    });
})
.catch(e => {
    CS.UI.alertAsync({
        text: e.message
    });
});
</color>


<seealso CS_Network.csdoc />
